 ### Data Structures
 The core data structure is the PhaseTree, a binary or n-ary tree where each node evaluates to a multiphase model [S1].
-*   **Leaf Node:** Represents a monophase SDF $f$. It is converted into a multiphase model with $n$ phases (where $n$ is the global number of phases in the scene or subtree) [S1].
-*   **Internal Node:** Represents an operator combining child nodes. It maintains the 1-Lipschitz property if its children do and the operator is Lipschitz-preserving [S1].
+*   **Leaf Node:** Represents a monophase SDF $f$ [S1]. It is converted into a multiphase model with $n$ phases using the Set $k$ conversion operator [S1].
+*   **Internal Node:** Represents an operator combining child nodes [S1]. It maintains the 1-Lipschitz property if its children do and the operator is Lipschitz-preserving [S1].
 *   **Phase Vector:** At any point $\mathbf{p}$, the state is defined by the vector $\Phi(\mathbf{p}) = [\phi_1(\mathbf{p}), \dots, \phi_n(\mathbf{p})]$ [S1].
 
